cff-version: 1.2.0
title: DCVigil Constitution Corpus
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, please cite it and the Digital Judiciary programme
  papers it instantiates.
type: dataset
version: 2.4.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
authors:
  - family-names: Kadambi
    given-names: Arun
  - family-names: Kuppuswamy
    given-names: Venkat
    affiliation: >-
      D'Amore-McKim School of Business, Northeastern University
abstract: >-
  An open 6,000-case conformance corpus for governing software change in
  multi-tenant data-centre monitoring, observability and AIOps platforms under a
  Digital Judiciary. A constitution of 108 provisions (17 absolute) across
  telemetry ingestion, automated remediation and physical actuation, tenant
  isolation, privileged-agent security, kernel and eBPF safety, telemetry
  integrity, change quality gates, agent resource budgets, AIOps model
  governance, supply chain, agent-authored code, data residency and redaction,
  audit evidence, operational windows, and governance of the judiciary itself.
  It is a superset of the released DCVigil pack: its twenty-nine provisions are
  reproduced with text and absolute flags unchanged, and five findings against
  them are filed as draft amendments rather than applied. Ground truth is
  computed from an executed trace. Ships a reference adjudication engine, 26
  conformance checks with a strengthened pressure-invariance check, a mutation
  matrix, and a four-pack profile comparison.
keywords:
  - compliance
  - precedent
  - policy-as-code
  - observability
  - AIOps
  - datacenter monitoring
  - conformance testing
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      When Retrieval Binds: Appraisal, Authenticity and Disposition in
      Automated Compliance Decisions
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Case-Base Formation for Precedential Constraint: Standing, Admission
      Rules, and the Reason Model
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
